*(iv) the tightening of eligibility of the DSP forces many people living with disability to rely on the lower rate under JobSeeker, entrenching poverty and disadvantage,* >> >> *(v) poverty is a political choice; and* > > *(b) calls on the Government to:* > >> *(i) abolish the punitive partner income test for the DSP, and* >> >> *(ii) raise the rate of income support payments as a matter of urgency\".*","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-9580","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2025-02-12/24"}
